Here is the commit message:
AMBARI-20712 - Parallel Requests With Intersecting Hosts
 Don't Block Correctly (jonathanhurley)

Here is the root cause:
The bug was caused by the inability of the system to correctly handle parallel requests that involve intersecting hosts. Specifically, the logic did not properly account for background commands, which should not block other requests. This oversight led to situations where commands that were meant to run in parallel were incorrectly blocked, resulting in delays and inefficiencies in command execution.

Here is the patch:
 import org.apache.ambari.server.agent.ActionQueue;
